  "//optionalDependencies": "Named here only so package-lock.json records them. lightningcss, @tailwindcss/oxide and sharp ship their native binary in a per-platform package, and a lock generated on macOS captures the darwin one alone — `npm ci` on the Linux instance then finds nothing to install and the Tailwind build dies on a missing .node file. npm skips these on macOS because of the os/cpu fields, so they cost developers nothing. Versions are exact: each binary package must match its parent's version, so bump them together.",
